@startuml seq-byo-key
title Bring-your-own vendor key → actor memory → snapshot

actor User
participant "serve" as serve
participant "brain b-<sid>" as brain
participant "Anthropic API" as api
database "GCS snapshot" as gcs

User -> serve : POST /v1/sessions {"apiKey":"sk-…"}\nor PUT /v1/sessions/{id}/key
serve -> brain : forward once (never stored server-side ✅,\nnever logged ✅, never an event ✅)
brain -> brain : apiKey held in process memory only
brain -> api : turn request with that key

== suspend ==
brain -> gcs : <b>memory image written to GCS</b>
note right of gcs #FFE4E4
  <b>F6</b>: the key is IN the snapshot, and so is any
  credential the paired hand pulled. Bucket read = secret read.
  Mitigation today: CMEK + bucket IAM. Real fix: F9.
end note

== resume ==
gcs -> brain : restore — key still in memory, no re-supply needed
@enduml
